## TRADE-OFF PRIORITY CHAIN

When design goals conflict, resolve along this priority chain (highest to lowest):

```
Accessibility > Safety (irreversible actions) > Readability > Consistency > Contextualization > Information Density > Aesthetic Exceptions > Feature Richness
```

**Example applications**:
- Contrast ratio (Accessibility) wins over brand color guidelines (Aesthetic)
- Confirmation dialog (Safety) wins over flow speed (Feature Richness)
- Legible font size (Readability) wins over fitting more content (Information Density)
- Following existing patterns (Consistency) wins over a "better" one-off solution (Contextualization)

If you deviate from this chain, document the reason explicitly.

---

## ERRORS AS SYSTEM FAILURE (Don Norman)

A core principle: **Errors are NEVER the user's fault.**

- **Slips** (user knows the right action but executes incorrectly): Prevent with constraints, confirmation, and undo
- **Mistakes** (user forms the wrong intention): Prevent with clear labeling, obvious affordances, and good conceptual models
- **Design response**: When an error occurs, the interface should explain what happened, why, and what to do next — without blame language
- **NEVER**: "You entered an invalid email" — **ALWAYS**: "This email format doesn't look right. Try name@example.com"

---

## PREDICTABILITY PRINCIPLE

The user must ALWAYS know:
1. **Where they are** — Screen title, breadcrumbs, active tab
2. **What they can do** — Visible buttons, clear affordances
3. **What will happen** — Descriptive labels ("Send Payment" not "Confirm")
4. **How to go back** — Back button, gesture, X to close

---

## PRE-CREATION CHECKLIST

Before creating any screen in Figma, answer:

- [ ] What is the SINGLE primary action of this screen?
- [ ] What is the visual hierarchy? (1st, 2nd, 3rd element)
- [ ] Does the spacing follow the 8px grid?
- [ ] Do touch targets have at least 44×44px?
- [ ] Is text contrast sufficient (4.5:1)?
- [ ] Does the user know how to go back?
- [ ] Is there enough breathing room between sections?
- [ ] Are all circular buttons ACTUALLY circular (width = height)?

---

### DESIGN SYSTEM THINKING

Before creating any screen, also answer:
- [ ] Does this screen use ONLY components/patterns already in the design system?
- [ ] If a new pattern is needed, is it general enough to be added to the system?
- [ ] Are design tokens (colors, spacing, type) used instead of hard-coded values?
- [ ] Has the screen been reviewed against the 7 pillars (Hierarchy, Contrast, Alignment, Proximity, Repetition, Whitespace, Unity)?

